      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "Blocking until there is evidence: as written this removes the dummy vision forward in the case it was added for.\n\nThe description says the dummy image \"only exists so that the vision tower stays in the autograd graph\". That is not what the maintainers recorded when the code was added. In #5938, hjh0119 answers: \"Add a dummy image to prevent deepspeed zero3 from hanging when training on a mixed multimodal/text dataset.\" #9639 spells out the mechanism for another template: under ZeRO the parameters are sharded and only all-gathered when a computation touches them, so a rank that skips the vision tower while another rank runs it leaves the second rank waiting inside an all-gather.\n\nWith this change that situation comes back in two ways:\n1. A frozen tower (the default `freeze_vit=True`) under ZeRO-3. The new condition needs a vision parameter with `requires_grad`, so a frozen tower skips the forward on text-only batches. ZeRO-3 shards frozen parameters too (LoRA with ZeRO-3 is the usual example), so a rank that does run the tower for an image batch waits for the rank that skipped it. #10214 keeps the tower out of the autograd graph, but it does not change which ranks take part in the all-gather.\n2. Evaluation and generation. `torch.is_grad_enabled()` is False under `no_grad`, so on a text-only batch the early return is taken even when the tower is trainable, while a rank with images still runs the tower.\n\nI could not reproduce either. I only have one small GPU, and the measurements in the description are from a single H200, where there is no other rank to wait for. So this is a request for evidence, not a proven regression: a 2-GPU ZeRO-3 run with `freeze_vit=True` where one rank receives a text-only batch and the other one with images, before and after the change, and the same through the evaluation loop.\n\nIf it does hang, this file already has an idiom for \"parameters are sharded\": `get_default_device_map` in `swift/model/utils.py` checks `is_deepspeed_zero3_enabled() or os.environ.get('ACCELERATE_USE_FSDP', 'False').lower() == 'true'`. Keeping the dummy forward whenever that holds, and skipping only otherwise, would keep the single-GPU and DDP speed-up and leave the sharded cases as they are:\n\n```python\nsharded = is_deepspeed_zero3_enabled() or os.environ.get('ACCELERATE_USE_FSDP', 'False').lower() == 'true'\nif not sharded and not (torch.is_grad_enabled() and any(p.requires_grad for p in visual.parameters())):\n    return inputs_embeds\n```\n\n(`is_deepspeed_zero3_enabled` is already imported in `base.py`.)\n\nOptional: #9104 describes a hang of the same family for a trainable tower under ZeRO-2 (a different template); the grad clause in your condition already keeps the dummy for training there. The helper is also shared by the glm, llava and qwen templates, so if the change stays in the shared function, the evidence should cover at least one template of each.\n",
